{{JPExclusive}}
'''Naughty Woody''' is a [[:Category:Typeless Enemies|Typeless]] enemy. It was added in [[Version 15.3 Update|Version 15.3]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Naughty Woody
|image = E 774.png
|first appearance = [[Assault! Naughty Woody]]
|money drop = 0¢ - 0¢
}}

==Enemy==
Naughty Woody isn't too much of a threat, but can be annoying nevertheless at higher strength magnifications where he gains a substantial amount of damage. Apart from that, its three-part multi-hits have decently high uptime and deliver guaranteed Slow/Knockback to whatever caught in their area of effect, up to a massive 2000 range, though they are not properly connected and have small blindspots between them.

==Strategy==
As with many animated enemy bases, Naughty Woody is still vulnerable to Surge Attacks and Explosions, or units that can withstand both the damage and status effects. Faster units can potentially enter the range of its first hit after while avoiding the second and quickly tear it down. Ranged units might not fare as well, as few can remain inside the blindspots, assuming if they get there.

